## Fixes in the commit

- F691 and F702: the new module apps/storytime/lib/teacher-lang.tsx holds TextRun,
  splitThaiRuns, and LanguageRuns with no "use client" directive, so the helpers work on the
  server and in the browser. lesson-flow.tsx imports LanguageRuns from it; week-view.tsx
  imports it and no longer imports from lesson-flow.tsx, so the week page ships no client
  chunk of the lesson flow. The test imports point at the new module.
- F692 and F701 (docs/runbooks/storytime-deploy.md, flag section only): the revision lookup
  command and the note that the tag URL has its own host move before list item 1; items 5 and
  6 begin with "When item 4 ran,"; item 3 adds "If another name differs, stop, give no
  traffic step, and report the difference to Daniel"; item 4 adds the case where the new
  build and the live revision both hold the flag (no off command; the new build goes to the
  traffic step 4 of this runbook after items 1 to 3); item 6 names "the traffic step 4 of
  this runbook", keeps the pinned phrase "traffic step (step 4)", and says only Daniel's go
  starts it; item 5 says the update command prints the name of the off revision. Every
  command, --no-traffic, the tags, Daniel's go, and the way back stay. No gcloud command ran.
- F693 (lesson-flow.tsx, week-view.tsx): LanguageRuns now wraps the Friday check item fields
  (sound, the picture and word circle lines, the answer lines, the word and letter write
  fields, the sort groups), the review strip card text, the graphemes of the element, the
  letter box letter, and the read-along and decodable titles. The visible text does not
  change.
- F694 (phase4-lesson-focus.test.tsx): the scroll suite removes the scrollIntoView stub in a
  suite-level afterEach, so a failed assertion cannot leak the defineProperty value; the
  shared afterEach keeps restoring the getBoundingClientRect spy. One boundary case pins the
  edge: a box top equal to window.innerHeight scrolls (the region is outside), one pixel less
  does not.

